<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  MasterClock — tr (Turkish)

  Mode names (Fischer, Byoyomi, Sudden Death…) and chess variant names are Kotlin literals rather
  than resources, so they stay in English by construction — see the notes in values/strings.xml.

  app_name and settings_app_version are left out on purpose: they are the product name.

  Turkish attaches its suffixes to words, and their vowels follow the word they attach to. A suffix
  is never put on a number placeholder here: the sentences are built so that "Oyuncu %d" or
  "Tur %d" reads correctly whatever the number is. The labels in tight rows (the settings tabs, the
  presets tabs, the Omni segments) are deliberately short.

  Translated without a native reviewer, like every language here except the French.
-->
